                        "entry_id": "1138d457-15e5-3dbb-9b9b-8c91c726a1e9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Alternative form of smutch (“a stain or smudge”)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "alt-of",
                            "alternative"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "aad4de10-4acc-441e-9a37-d442c6b2bb6e",
                                "sense_id": "6e70a7d9-2dcd-304e-b6c5-07d81e5812b3",
                                "text": "Suppose an artist, after having completed such a picture, in a moment of intoxication, goes into his studio, takes his brush, dips it into black paint, and applies it thereto. Only one smouch and the work of months is destroyed!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "16cc61b8-2a83-4f0b-bab3-1c77b8c2ccd7",
                                "sense_id": "6e70a7d9-2dcd-304e-b6c5-07d81e5812b3",
                                "text": "[…]and on her breast a baby, wet as she, smiling and cooing, but with a great crimson smouch on its tiny shoulder."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
